# k stays below a 32-bit limit, so k++ cannot leave 32 bits: one 32-bit addition and the comparison with the limit.
# HOT-LABEL: steps by 1
# HOT: Int32 b@[[k]] = Phi(
# HOT: Int32 b@[[masked]] = BitAnd(b@{{*}}, b@[[k]], {{*}}:BitAnd)
# HOT-NEXT: Branch(b@[[masked]], Terminal, {{*}}:StrictEq)
# HOT: Int32 b@[[next]] = Add(b@[[k]], $1(b@{{*}}), {{*}}:Increment)
# HOT-NEXT: Int32 b@[[goesOn]] = GreaterThan(b@{{*}}, b@[[next]], {{*}}:Less)
# HOT-NEXT: Branch(b@[[goesOn]], Terminal, {{*}}:Less)
# The count of matches cannot outrun k, so it is an integer too: one is added to it on the arm of a match. It may stand one step above 32 bits, so it has 64.
# HOT: Int64 b@{{*}} = Add(b@{{*}}, $1(b@{{*}}), {{*}}:Increment)
# HOT-LABEL: end of loop
# Nothing tests for overflow, widens the counter or converts it, and no double is added.
